@@ -3,6 +3,13 @@
 Minimal link shortener.
 
 - `POST /shorten` with `{"url": "..."}` -> `201 {"code": "..."}`
-- `GET /<code>` -> `302` redirect
+- `POST /shorten` also accepts optional `"ttl_seconds"` (integer, 1 to 10 years); the link expires after that many seconds
+- `GET /<code>` -> `302` redirect, `404` if unknown, `410 Gone` if expired
+
+## Changelog
+
+### v1.1
+- Added optional link expiry (`ttl_seconds`, new nullable `expires_at` column, automatic idempotent migration for v1 databases).
+- Fixed: a newly generated code that collided with an existing one silently overwrote that link (`INSERT OR REPLACE`). Inserts are now strict and collisions are retried.
 
 Run tests: `python -m pytest`
